{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And Jacob was incensed and quarreled with Laban.</b> At first he gave him permission to search, for he said, \"With whomever you find your elohim,\" and he said, \"Recognize before our kinsmen what I have with me,\" and how would he find if he did not search and feel about? But at first he was concerned that perhaps one of the women or the servants had stolen his elohim, and now when he saw that they were not with them, his anger burned, for he said, I did not lose his elohim; rather, he is seeking a pretext against me. He said to him: Why did you pursue me? As a man pursues a thief — yet you found nothing of all the vessels of your household with me. And it would have been fitting for me to take from you whatever I could, for you changed my wages ten times, and yet you would claim from me for animals torn by beasts and I would pay you — unjustly."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:37:53.021807959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}